                <pb facs="1137" n="1041" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg1041"/>

                <head>No. 495.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baker to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-02-27"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 27, 1879</date>.
                        (Received March 24.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 98.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: At about 4 p.m. on the 25th instant General
                    Guzman Blanco arrived in Caracas. The town was duly decorated and embannered for
                    the occasion, and the <hi rendition="#italic">entrée</hi> was accompanied by a
                    movement of the people, discharges of cannon, and explosion of rockets.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JEHU BAKER.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
